description:
Design a 16-bit to 32-bit sign extension module. This module takes a 16-bit input and extends it to a 32-bit output, maintaining the sign of the input by replicating the most significant bit (the sign bit) of the 16-bit value across the upper 16 bits of the output. If the sign bit is 1 (indicating a negative number), the upper bits will be filled with 1s; if it is 0 (indicating a positive number), they will be filled with 0s.
module top_module(
	input [15:0] src,
	output [31:0] out
);

