description:
Design a circuit that demonstrates bit shifting operations. The module takes a 4-bit input called ShiftVal and produces two outputs: a right-shifted result (RSRes) and a left-shifted result (LSRes) of a reference value, -55. The right shift is an arithmetic shift, preserving the sign of the reference value, while the left shift extends the value by moving bits to the left. The outputs are signed, with RSRes being 8 bits wide and LSRes being 15 bits wide.
module top_module(
    ShiftVal,
    RSRes,
    LSRes
);

code:
