description:
Design a clock divider circuit that generates a square wave output signal. The output, clkout, toggles with a frequency that is half of the frequency of the input clock signal, clkin, based on the parameter 'n'. The module employs a counter 'cnt' to count the clock cycles of clkin, resetting after reaching n-1, and sets clkout to HIGH for the first half of the count and LOW for the second half, effectively creating a divided clock output.
module top_module(
    clkin,clkout
);

code:
module top_module(
    clkin,clkout
);input clkin;
    output reg clkout;
    parameter n = 32;
    parameter m = 4;
    reg[m:0] cnt;
always @(posedge clkin) begin
    if(cnt>=n-1) cnt<=5'b00000;
    else cnt<=cnt+1;
    if(cnt<n/2) clkout<=1;
    else clkout<=0;
end
endmodule

